cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the LOD-AM data model or vocabularies, please cite them as below."
type: software
title: "LOD-AM knowledge graph: data model, vocabularies and checks"
abstract: >-
  Data model of LOD-AM (Linked Open Data for Ancient Metallurgy), a one-person
  research project on Linked Open Data for archaeometallurgy: modelling
  conventions on CIDOC CRM 7.1.3, CRMsci, CRMarchaeo, Allotrope (AFO), FaBiO
  and PROV-O, SHACL shapes, local vocabularies, a worked example, SPARQL
  queries and the checks that hold all of it to the source ontologies.
authors:
  - family-names: Fricke
    given-names: Fabian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3223-2079"
    website: "https://lod-am.net/about/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/LOD-AM/knowledge-graph"
url: "https://lod-am.net/"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
keywords:
  - Linked Open Data
  - archaeometallurgy
  - CIDOC CRM
  - data model
  - SHACL
